// Shared Syncthing ignore patterns for this vault. This file IS synced and
// committed; the per-device .stignore is not (Syncthing never syncs .stignore).
// On every machine, .stignore must exist and contain exactly the line:
//   #include .stignore-shared
// Order on a NEW machine (README step 5): let the first sync deliver this file,
// then write .stignore and reload the ignores — an #include of a file that does
// not exist yet is an error and stops the folder from syncing at all. Nothing
// leaks meanwhile: a fresh machine has none of the files below. On a machine
// that already holds them (the automation host with its .git), write .stignore
// BEFORE adding the folder.
// A leading / anchors the pattern to the folder root. Syntax:
// https://docs.syncthing.net/users/ignoring.html

// Your identity note — the bases read the current user from it, so it must
// differ per member. Without it every base shows one "create _local/me.md" group.
/_local

// Your Templater folder: the copy of shared_templates/ the setup made after
// checking it (README step 7). A template is JavaScript that Templater runs by
// itself on every note you create, so only the copy checked on this machine
// runs — never something that just arrived over the network.
/local_templates

// Per-user Obsidian configuration: themes, hotkeys, plugin choices, plugin
// data files (which can hold tokens), and workspace layout.
/.obsidian

// Per-user Claude Code configuration and session state.
/.claude/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/projects
/.claude/skills/about-me
/.claude/handoffs

// Claudian plugin state (sessions churn on every message).
/.claudian

// The vault's git repository lives on the automation host only. File-level
// sync corrupts git repos, so this must never be shared.
/.git

// Obsidian's own trash and the logs of the scheduled jobs (host-local noise).
/.trash
/other-files/logs

// Your own code checkouts. Per-user in full: they are separate repositories,
// which never sync file by file. The folder may not exist on every machine.
/external-projects

// Optional private items: same conventions as projects-tasks-notes/, never
// synced. private.base is me.base pointed at that folder (setup-member skill).
/private-projects-tasks-notes
/private.base

// OS and Python cruft. (?d) lets Syncthing delete these when they block a
// directory removal.
(?d).DS_Store
(?d)Thumbs.db
(?d)__pycache__
